# Lunduke Linux Kernel config delta: 7.2.6-lcos12 → 7.2.6-lcos13
# Built 2026-10-03 — config and packaging only; no kernel debs, no ISO bake.
#
# Base is the frozen lcos12 config (5317e83). lcos12 files are not edited.
# olddefconfig: Linux 7.2.6, gcc-14, LOCALVERSION= (same finalize as the build script).
#
# Intentional hardware (y where Omarchy 7.2.5 built it in, m where Omarchy used a module):
#   Intel pinctrl/GPIO: PINCTRL, GPIOLIB, PINCTRL_INTEL, Bay Trail, Cherryview,
#     and the rest of Omarchy's Intel pinctrl block except Lunar/Panther Lake.
#   LPSS, DesignWare I2C (core/platform/PCI), SERIAL_DEV_BUS.
#   UART BT: BT_HCIUART_SERDEV, INTEL, BCM, RTL, QCA.
#   MOUSE_PS2_ELANTECH=y, INTEL_HID_EVENT=m, INTEL_VBTN=m.
#   Intel SOF/SoundWire *_MACH set Omarchy enables (not the nocodec board, not AVS).
#   AMD ACP3x/5x/6x and the ACP machine drivers Omarchy enables that lcos12 lacked.
#   ACP7X left off (platform driver, not one of the named ACP symbols or a _MACH).
#   USB_USBNET, USB_RTL8152, USB_NET_CDCETHER, USB_NET_RNDIS_HOST, USB_NET_AQC111, ALX (all m).
#   Realtek RTSX PCI/USB + MMC_REALTEK PCI/USB (m).
#   Short hwmon set, INT340X_THERMAL, POWERCAP=y, INTEL_RAPL=m, INTEL_IDLE=y,
#     CPU_IDLE_GOV_TEO=y, AMD_PMC=m, AMD_PMF=m.
#   IWLMLD=m (IWLWIFI and IWLMVM left m).
#   In-tree Surface Aggregator (hub, registry, tablet-switch, dtx, hotplug,
#     platform-profile), SURFACE_HID, SURFACE_KBD, BATTERY_SURFACE, CHARGER_SURFACE.
#   Vendor hotkeys: MSI_WMI, MSI_EC, LG_LAPTOP, SONY_LAPTOP, ACPI_TOSHIBA,
#     FUJITSU_LAPTOP, SAMSUNG_LAPTOP, EEEPC_WMI (m).
#
# Not in Linux 7.2.6 (not invented as a different driver):
#   CONFIG_PINCTRL_LUNARLAKE
#   CONFIG_PINCTRL_PANTHERLAKE
# CONFIG_PINCTRL_INTEL_PLATFORM left unset. In 7.2.6 that symbol is the
# Lunar Lake / Nova Lake / Panther Lake pinctrl driver.
#
# Kept off: SURFACE_3_POWER_OPREGION, SURFACE_GPE, SURFACE_PRO3_BUTTON,
#   CONFIG_RUST, Android binder (C and Rust), HSA_AMD, zram, module signing,
#   lockdown. X86_PKG_TEMP_THERMAL left m. Existing SOF PCI, HDA Intel,
#   AMD SOF_MACH, and AMD PS_MACH were not removed.
#
# Dependency fill so the requested symbols survive olddefconfig (not extra boards):
#   SPI/SPI_MASTER, SND_SOC_INTEL_USER_FRIENDLY_LONG_NAMES, SND_SOC_INTEL_CATPT,
#   MFD_ARIZONA_I2C + MFD_WM5102, I2C_DESIGNWARE_BAYTRAIL, IIO (ACPI_TOSHIBA),
#   CHROME_PLATFORMS + CROS_EC (RV_RT5682 machine only; Chrome EC sub-devices
#   that merely default-on were turned back off),
#   CRYPTO_DEV_CCP + CRYPTO_DEV_CCP_DD + CRYPTO_DEV_SP_PSP + TEE + AMDTEE
#   + AMD_SFH_HID (AMD_PMF). Codec/select symbols follow the machine drivers.
#   Extra USB-net drivers that default y under USB_USBNET were turned back off.
#   VIDEO_CAMERA_SENSOR stayed off (it defaulted y once COMMON_CLK appeared).
#
# CRITICAL: # CONFIG_RUST is not set (No Forced Rust). No Rust Android binder.
# Toolchain probe lines (CC/AS/LD/pahole/rustc) match the machine that ran
# olddefconfig. A later olddefconfig on the Debian builder may refresh them.
#
# Unified diff of full .config follows.
#
